# Netlify reads this file from the publish directory, so it applies under both
# of the wirings netlify.toml describes (base = repo root, or base = site/).
# Redirect rules in a netlify.toml would take precedence over it; neither of
# ours defines any.
#
# The site answers on two hostnames: the custom domain and the Netlify
# subdomain it was first deployed to. Both served 200, so the whole site
# existed twice for a crawler. Every page carries a canonical pointing at the
# custom domain, which is enough for Google to consolidate, but the duplicate
# still gets crawled and can still be linked. This makes the subdomain a
# permanent redirect instead.
#
# The rule matches that exact host, so Netlify's deploy previews and branch
# deploys — deploy-preview-N--<site>.netlify.app — are untouched and stay
# browsable. `301!` forces the redirect: without the bang, a request for a
# path that exists as a static file (which is all of them) would be served
# rather than redirected.

https://vaavkitchenandcaterers.netlify.app/*  https://vaavkitchenandcaterers.com/:splat  301!
